WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.469
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.970
you know from
"Friday Night Lights,"

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.839
"Nashville," and "Dirty John."

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.373
She stars in
the critically acclaimed show

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:08.541
"The White Lotus."

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.843
The first full season
is streaming on HBO Max.

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:11.844
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:14.647
-Just lift it.
-Push it. Tilt.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:17.817
Oh, oh.
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:18.952
-Ohh.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:21.855
-Oh, God.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.457
-Are you okay, Paula?
-No.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.958
-Alright,
I'm gonna start my Zoom,

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:27.326
and, you guys, if you're
gonna stay in here,

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:29.262
you have to be totally silent.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.896
Okay?
And stay out of the frame.

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:33.033
-Mom, you look deranged.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.100
-It's alright.
I have a filter for that.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.503
Oh [bleep]

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.639
-Please welcome back to the show
Connie Britton.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.140
How are you, Connie?

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.276
-Hi, Seth.
I'm so good.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.977
How are you?
-I'm wonderful.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:48.447
Congratulations for being in
the show of the summer,

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.049
the most talked-about show
of the summer.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:53.553
It must be exciting because,
you know, I feel like I --

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.855
You know, I'm such a fan of your
work on "Friday Night Lights,"

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.824
which I feel like is a show that
people just kind of discovered

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:00.727
maybe a little bit
after the fact.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.361
It must be so fun
to be in something

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:04.564
that everybody is watching
in real time.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.598
-It is.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.767
It's a fascinating experience

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:11.104
because, you know,
particularly in the world now,

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:14.173
we're all bingers now
and it's all --

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:15.542
you know, it's all --

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:18.444
There's so much conversation
around the shows,

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.713
the shows of the season,
the shows of the season.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:24.684
And to be --
Now I'm the conversation.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.252
We're the conversation,
"The White Lotus."

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.188
I mean, honestly,
it's really Mike White.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:31.257
Mike White is the brilliant
creator of "The White Lotus."

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.860
And this is all his brainchild.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.095
We're just like little pawns,

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:39.131
little robots
in his crazy, crazy world.

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:41.267
But it's fascinating
to think about

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.070
what it is that hits
the zeitgeist.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.740
You know, like, why are people
so interested in this show?

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.842
You know, I mean, like,
what do you like about it, Seth?

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:53.846
I think it just hits home
in a way where it makes it okay

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:57.450
for people to see themselves
in a not-very-nice light.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.153
-Well, there's a lot of --
It ticks a lot of boxes for me.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:02.889
Let's just start with,
in today's world,

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.323
where things move really fast,

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:08.061
if you give me a six-episode
season, I'm super psyched.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:11.030
Right off the bat, I know I'm
gonna have the time for it.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.565
I mean, for people
who haven't watched,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:13.899
I'm not giving anything away.

00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:15.768
The first five minutes
of the show,

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:19.105
they basically tell you that
someone dies at this resort.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.141
So there now you got me
on the hook.

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.277
And, you know,
the cast is so fantastic.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.746
But you are right --
Like, there's this singular

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.381
Mike White writing style

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.317
that complete--
reveals itself immediately.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:34.486
And it is just so much fun
to watch you all

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:36.321
play around with those scripts.

00:02:36.321 --> 00:02:38.657
-And, you know, I think, like,
right now in the culture,

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:41.761
there's so much conversation
going on.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:45.331
We really are assessing
ourselves as a culture,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.800
as you know, because you're
at the forefront of that.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.804
And so to be able to do that
in a satirical way

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:55.007
where it takes --

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:57.443
We can clearly look
at these characters

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:00.846
and see that they are,
for the most part, hideous.

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:06.619
And yet -- And so we can freely,
you know, look at ourselves

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.389
because we have to be better
than they are.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:10.890
And yet -- And we can laugh,

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.992
and, you know,
that's a really good way

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.028
to make a little commentary

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.962
about what's happening
in the world.

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:19.932
-Hideous people in pretty
fantastic surroundings.

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:23.870
You got to shoot this
at the Four Seasons in Maui

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.905
in the middle of a pandemic.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:29.175
This strikes me as maybe
the best possible place

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.510
to go to work.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.780
-You know what?
I have to agree with you.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.081
-Yeah.
-The Four Seasons --

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:38.550
I mean, Maui is the best
possible place to go to work

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.287
and particularly
in the middle of a pandemic.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:44.490
I was already -- You know, I'm
such a huge fan of Mike White's.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.926
I was already on board,
you know, minute one.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:49.195
But then he said,
"We're shooting in Maui."

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.763
And I said,
"Oh, you're so brilliant.

00:03:51.763 --> 00:03:53.866
You're more brilliant
than I even thought you were.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.135
Yes, I will come,
happily and gladly."

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.771
And then we got there,
and it's like "Ahhh!"

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.072
You know, we'd all been
in quarantine

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.307
for however many months.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.709
And it's so beautiful
and magical,

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:06.245
and we had the whole hotel
to ourselves for a while,

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.648
and that was really amazing.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:11.718
And then we realized
we couldn't leave.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:14.553
-Yeah.
-It was weird.

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:18.958
And I was like, "COVID,
you're making this weird.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:22.094
How are you making Maui
weird for us?

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:23.929
What is that about?"

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:25.397
And it's like,

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:29.969
"I can't go to the waterfall
if I have a day off?"

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.037
"No, no, you can't go to
the waterfall on the day off."

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:34.974
And so then it became
this really hilarious thing

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.242
where we were sort of like,

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.578
"We're in the most beautiful
place in the world,"

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.447
and also, "I want to go
to the waterfall,"

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.082
and then, "Am I becoming

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.351
the actual character
that I'm playing?"

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.752
It became very meta.

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:49.222
It was very like,
what's happening?

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.490
Who am I?

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.458
-Who would want
to hear you complain

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.560
about being trapped in Maui,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.396
at the Four Seasons in Maui,
no less?

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:59.732
-Right, right.
Turns out nobody. Nobody.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.467
-You play the mother
of teenagers,

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.971
who are mortified by everything
you do on the show.

00:05:05.971 --> 00:05:08.341
I believe your son is 10 now.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.608
Is that an age where --

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.744
Is he capable of being mortified
by you yet?

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:14.280
-He's not there yet,
thank goodness.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.950
10 is a really cute, good age.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.421
But I will tell you --
Here's what they don't tell you

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:24.256
about where that sort of
mortification comes from,

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:29.095
and the answer is, particularly
during a pandemic, television,

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:32.197
specifically the Disney Channel.

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:34.400
-No!
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.170
Seth, there are shows
on the Disney Channel --

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.872
Like, they're always
called people's names,

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:46.846
like "Jessie" or "Ricky --
Ricky, Dicky, &amp; Dawn."

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:49.481
And there might be another one
in there, too.

00:05:49.481 --> 00:05:52.819
-Okay.
-And these are like --

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:56.021
They are these shows that, like,
the kids love,

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:57.523
for whatever reason.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:06:00.226
Eyob will watch them on a loop.

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.760
The same --

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.929
And I said, "Are you watching
that show again?"

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:06.566
And he's like, "Yeah, I mean, I
already watched the full season.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:07.967
So I'm just rewatching it."

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:10.636
But the thing is,
then he starts, you know,

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:13.306
when we're talking,
he starts talking to me

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:16.308
in these kind of quippy ways

00:06:16.308 --> 00:06:19.278
that I can tell
he's now emulating

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.780
Disney Channel characters.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.548
And I'm like,
"This is the beginning.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:25.351
This is the beginning
of him being --"

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:28.121
-This is on you,
Ricky, Dicky, and Dawn.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:32.357
-This is on you, Ricky, Dicky,
and Dawn, and Mickey Mouse.

00:06:32.357 --> 00:06:34.627
-Real quick before we go,

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:37.563
you worked with one of
my favorite people in the world,

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:39.065
Jennifer Coolidge.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:43.469
And it just must have
been a dream.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.805
-Jennifer Coolidge
is a national treasure,

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:49.475
and I'm so glad that we now can
all just acknowledge that fully

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:52.511
when we see her brilliant work
in this show.

00:06:52.511 --> 00:06:54.012
And I'm obsessed with her,

00:06:54.012 --> 00:06:55.881
and I was recently down
in New Orleans.

00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:57.182
And she has a house
in New Orleans

00:06:57.182 --> 00:06:58.617
and she invited me over.

00:06:58.617 --> 00:07:00.452
And I was like,
"There's no way I'm missing

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:03.822
going to Jennifer Coolidge's
house in New Orleans."

00:07:03.822 --> 00:07:07.659
And I was sort of doing
other things all day.

00:07:07.659 --> 00:07:10.162
And she texted me.
She goes, "You have to --

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:12.965
No matter what, even if
it's late, you have to come

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:16.535
because I feel like the spirits
are really strong tonight."

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:18.871
And I was like, "You are right,
Jennifer Coolidge.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.673
Of course I have to come

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:22.842
if the spirits are really strong
at your house."

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:24.110
So I went to her house,

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:27.446
and she has the most
unbelievably gorgeous house

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.081
in New Orleans.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:32.184
I mean, it feels like
it's like a full city block.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:35.321
And so I get there
and I'm waiting at the gate

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:38.123
and I text her
and I'm like, "I'm here."

00:07:38.123 --> 00:07:40.293
And I think
a full five minutes passed,

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.694
and then she finally
texted me back,

00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:43.763
and she's like, "Oh, great!"

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:45.397
And then another
five minutes passed

00:07:45.397 --> 00:07:47.700
when she finally came out
to the gate to let me in,

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.635
because there was no way
actually in

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:52.771
and there was a big,
brooding gate.

00:07:52.771 --> 00:07:58.578
And so then I walked into
the house, and everything --

00:07:58.578 --> 00:08:00.779
There is no electrical light on.

00:08:00.779 --> 00:08:02.848
It is all candlelight.

00:08:02.848 --> 00:08:06.118
And it is the most beautiful,

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:11.590
perfectly, perfectly decorated
Victorian house,

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.158
completely candlelit.

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:15.194
I mean, the candelabras
were candlelit.

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:16.829
Everything was candlelight.

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:22.067
And it was like walking into
a house from like the 1800s

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:23.269
but also a haunted house.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:25.238
Like, I couldn't decide
what the vibe was.

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:28.173
And then her dining room table
had all these wine bottles on it

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:30.509
and she was like,
"Do you want wine?"

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:33.111
And I'm like,
"Of course I want wine."

00:08:33.111 --> 00:08:34.680
And she goes,
"And we have pizza."

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.116
And so we went back
to her back terrace

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:40.219
and ate pizza and drank wine
until 1:00 in the morning

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:41.721
waiting for the spirits
to show up,

00:08:41.721 --> 00:08:44.322
which they didn't quite do,

00:08:44.322 --> 00:08:46.492
but it really didn't matter,
because I got to, like,

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:48.627
be at Jennifer Coolidge's
amazing house.

00:08:48.627 --> 00:08:51.496
-Maybe she was the spirit
the whole time.

00:08:51.496 --> 00:08:53.398
-She is the spirit.
-She is the spirit.

00:08:53.398 --> 00:08:54.834
She's a good spirit.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:58.037
-She is the spirit, and that's
the answer to the question, yes.

00:08:58.037 --> 00:08:59.972
-Congratulations so much
on the show.

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:01.440
It's always so lovely
to see you,

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.708
and hopefully next time
you can be here in person.

00:09:03.708 --> 00:09:05.944
-I know. I can't wait.
I really can't wait for that.

00:09:05.944 --> 00:09:07.113
Thanks, Seth.

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:08.881
-The full first season
of "The White Lotus"

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:10.382
is streaming on HBO Max.

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:11.851
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

